<title>CANADA: Patheon signs Medicis Pharma.</title>
<headline>Patheon signs Medicis Pharma.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Patheon Inc said on Thursday it has signed contracts with Phoenix-based Medicis Pharmaceutical Corp to manufature topical steroid brands Lidex and Synalar.</p>
<p>Medicis recently completed the acquisition of these brands from Syntex (U.S.A.) Inc and its affiliates.</p>
<p>Medicis is now conducting an aggressive sampling and promotional campaign for the drugs targeting dermatologists across the United States and Canada.</p>
<p>Patheon said according to projections based on historical demand, the contracts should provide annual sales in the C$3 million to C$4 million range.</p>
<p>The company will manufacture the compounds will be done at Patheon's Mississauga facility and is scheduled to start in the second quarter of this fiscal year.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
